CAMBER — Commissioning, Analytics & M&V for Building Energy Re-tuning
Copyright 2026 The CAMBER authors

This product includes software for analyzing Building Automation System (BAS)
trend data. Its algorithms are reimplemented from public standards (ASHRAE
Guideline 36, Guideline 14, Standard 55, Standard 211; IPMVP; PNNL Building
Re-tuning; NIST APAR). No third-party source code is included.

CAMBER redistributes no datasets. The dataset catalog (camber/datasets/catalog.json)
records where open building datasets are published, under which licence, and
their checksums; `camber datasets fetch` downloads each file from its publisher
onto the user's machine. The data remains under its publisher's licence, which
the user accepts by downloading it; cite the publisher as the catalog entry
states.

camber/refrigerant.py carries the ancillary vapour-pressure coefficients for R-134a, R-22 and
R-32 as published in CoolProp 8.0.0 (http://www.coolprop.org; Bell, Wronski, Quoilin & Lemort
2014, doi:10.1021/ie4033999), Copyright (c) 2012-2018 Ian H. Bell and other CoolProp developers,
used under the MIT License. The R-410A and CO2 coefficients are those published by Lemmon (2003)
and Span & Wagner (1996). CoolProp itself is not a dependency.

The test suite includes the NIST Statistical Reference Dataset "Norris" (36 rows; a
U.S. Government work, not subject to copyright in the United States) to check CAMBER's
regression statistics against NIST's certified values.
